-## 3. `only_zero_transport` — Lemma 9.1(v), corrected form (referee's sketch)
-
-```lean
-theorem only_zero_transport {K : Type*} [Field K]
-    (G : (Fin 2 → K) ≃ₗ[K] (Fin 2 → K)) :
-    G '' ({0} : Set (Fin 2 → K)) = {0}
-```
-
-**Paper:** Lemma `lem:lifting`, item (v) addendum.  The exact
-computation is done at the $K_5$-point; the chart points are reached by
-the rescaling $u \mapsto \theta u$ with $\theta^7 = 1/a_{8,14}$ at the
-$K_5$-point.  This acts on $(t_1,t_2)$ by *some* $G \in \mathrm{GL}_2$
-(in the pivot-free basis, $G = \mathrm{diag}(\theta^9,\theta^{10})$ —
-the false "common scalar" wording from Round 5 was removed in v17).
-The minors transform by nonzero row factors and by
-$\mathrm{Sym}^5 G$, so rank 6, and hence the conclusion $t = 0$, is
-invariant; Galois conjugation over $K_5(\theta)$ reaches all 35
-points.
-
-**What the Lean proof does:** the image of $\{0\}$ under any linear
-automorphism is $\{0\}$ — i.e. "only $t = 0$" is a statement about the
-zero vector, which no $G \in \mathrm{GL}_2$ can move.  This is why the
-corrected lemma no longer needs the (false) common-scalar claim: the
-transport only ever has to preserve the *conclusion* $t = 0$, and every
-linear automorphism does.
