+## Characteristic
+
+`t_zero_case_char` needs only `2 ≠ 0` and `12 ≠ 0`, and `t_zero_case_fails_char3` is a counterexample
+in characteristic 3. So Lemma 9.1(iv)'s phrase "characteristic-free" should read "valid in every
+characteristic other than 2 and 3". The end-to-end theorem assumes `CharZero`.
+
+## What is still *not* formalized
+
+* **GGHV Proposition 4.3.** It is an explicit assumption of the whole paper (source-gated, §2).
+* **The classification of top layers** (Proposition 6.1, via the Riemann existence theorem and
+  Frobenius counting, `belyi_counts_m357.py`): that every solution of E5 with the vertex conditions
+  is a torus image of one of the five K₅ points. Mathlib has no dessins d'enfants or Riemann
+  existence theorem. `no_completion_K5` is therefore stated for top layers in the K₅ orbit, and
+  `top_layer_E5` checks that this orbit really consists of E5 solutions.
+* **Irreducibility of 𝒲 over ℚ** (Theorem 6.2(i)). The Lean statement no longer needs it: it
+  quantifies over every root `w` directly.
 
